const lessons = [
{title:'Người nổi tiếng muốn gặp',group:'Con người',page:3,topic:'Describe a famous person you would like to meet.',cues:['Who this person is','Why you want to meet them','Why they are famous','What you would do if you met them'],notes:['Taylor Swift · singer','songs → memories','ask about songwriting','nervous → grateful'],vi:'Giới thiệu ca sĩ → lý do yêu thích → một kỷ niệm nghe nhạc → điều muốn hỏi khi gặp.',tip:'Dùng câu điều kiện để nói về cuộc gặp chưa xảy ra: If I met her, I would…',vocab:['look up to|ngưỡng mộ','put feelings into words|diễn tả cảm xúc thành lời','in person|trực tiếp, ngoài đời'],answer:`I’d like to talk about Taylor Swift, a singer and songwriter I would love to meet. I first heard her music when I was at school, and some of her songs remind me of that time in my life.
She is famous for her music and live performances, but what interests me most is the way she tells stories. Even when a song describes something I have never experienced, I can usually understand the feeling behind it. I sometimes listen to her music on my way to work because it helps me relax before a busy day.
If I had the chance to meet her, I would ask how she turns an ordinary experience into a song. I often struggle to put my feelings into words, so I would be interested in her approach. I would also tell her about a song that helped me through a difficult week.
Of course, I would probably feel quite nervous at first. I wouldn’t want to ask too many questions or take up all her time. A short conversation and a photograph together would be enough. For me, meeting someone whose work has become part of my everyday life would be a really special experience.`},
{title:'Người thân bạn ngưỡng mộ',group:'Con người',page:4,topic:'Describe someone in your family who you really admire.',cues:['Your relationship with this person','Your first memories of them','How often you see them','Why you admire them'],notes:['mother · patient','first memory → bicycle','every weekend','mistake at work → advice'],vi:'Mẹ → kỷ niệm tập xe → gặp cuối tuần → một lần mẹ giúp bạn bình tĩnh.',tip:'Đừng chỉ liệt kê tính từ. Một câu chuyện nhỏ sẽ làm rõ vì sao bạn ngưỡng mộ người đó.',vocab:['stay calm|giữ bình tĩnh','step by step|từng bước một','look at the bigger picture|nhìn vấn đề rộng hơn'],answer:`The person in my family I admire most is my mother. She is a quiet person, but she has had a huge influence on how I deal with problems.
One of my earliest memories of her is learning to ride a bicycle. I was afraid of falling, so she walked beside me and held the back of the bike. When I finally managed to ride on my own, she looked even happier than I did. That memory sums up the kind of person she is: patient and always ready to help.
We don’t live together now, but I usually visit her at weekends. We cook lunch, talk about our week and sometimes go for a short walk. If I’m busy, I call her in the evening instead.
What I admire most is her ability to stay calm. For example, when I made a mistake at work, I felt terrible and wanted to avoid talking about it. She encouraged me to explain what had happened and think about how to fix it, step by step.
She has taught me that being responsible doesn’t mean never making mistakes. It means being honest and learning from them. That is a lesson I still use almost every day.`},
{title:'Người có ảnh hưởng đến bạn',group:'Con người',page:5,topic:'Describe a person who has been an important influence in your life.',cues:['Who they are and how long you have known them','Why you chose this person','How they influenced your life','How you feel about them'],notes:['English teacher · ten years','afraid of mistakes','one-minute talks','confidence → work'],vi:'Thầy tiếng Anh → nỗi sợ nói sai → bài tập nói ngắn → thay đổi trong công việc.',tip:'Thể hiện sự thay đổi bằng used to… but now…; dùng quá khứ cho câu chuyện và hiện tại cho ảnh hưởng còn lại.',vocab:['build confidence|xây dựng sự tự tin','speak up|mạnh dạn lên tiếng','make progress|tiến bộ'],answer:`I’d like to describe my former English teacher, Mr Minh. I first met him about ten years ago, when I was still at school. Although he only taught me for one year, his advice has stayed with me.
At that time, I was very shy about speaking English. I could usually understand the lesson, but I was afraid of giving a wrong answer in front of other people. As a result, I hardly ever spoke in class.
Mr Minh noticed this and gave me a simple task. Every week, I had to talk for one minute about something familiar, such as my favourite food or my weekend. He didn’t interrupt every time I made a mistake. Instead, he listened and gave me one or two things to improve afterwards.
After a few months, I realised that I could communicate even when my grammar wasn’t perfect. That helped me build confidence, not just in English but in other situations too. Now, when I need to speak up in a meeting, I still remember his advice to focus on the message.
I feel very grateful to him. He didn’t suddenly make me an excellent speaker, but he helped me stop avoiding difficult situations and start making progress.`},
{title:'Một chuyến đi đáng nhớ',group:'Chuyến đi',page:6,topic:'Describe a journey that you remember well.',cues:['Where you went','How you travelled','Why you went','Why you remember the journey well'],notes:['Da Nang → Hue','train · friends','weekend break','sea view · shared snacks'],vi:'Đi tàu ra Huế → mục đích nghỉ cuối tuần → cảnh biển và trò chuyện → hành trình đáng nhớ hơn dự kiến.',tip:'Đề journey tập trung vào quá trình di chuyển. Hãy dành nhiều chi tiết cho những gì xảy ra trên đường.',vocab:['take a break|nghỉ ngơi một chút','along the coast|dọc bờ biển','lose track of time|quên mất thời gian'],answer:`A journey I remember especially well was a train trip from Da Nang to Hue with two close friends. We went there a few years ago because we wanted a short break after a busy period at work.
We chose the train because none of us wanted to drive. At first, I thought the journey would simply be a way to get to Hue. However, it became one of the best parts of the whole trip.
We left in the morning and found seats near a window. As the train travelled along the coast, we could see the sea on one side and green hills on the other. I took a few photographs, but after a while I put my phone away and just enjoyed the view.
My friends had brought sandwiches and fruit, so we shared our food and talked about everything from work to our old school days. We were enjoying ourselves so much that we almost lost track of time.
I remember this journey because it made me slow down. Usually, I’m in a hurry to reach my destination, but that day I enjoyed the time on the way. It reminded me that travelling with the right people can make even a simple journey feel special.`},
{title:'Chiếc điện thoại đầu tiên',group:'Đồ vật',page:7,topic:'Describe your first mobile phone.',cues:['Where and when you got it','When you bought it','Why you bought it','How you felt when you first got it'],notes:['small shop · age sixteen','saved pocket money','contact parents','independence · simple games'],vi:'Mua bằng tiền tiết kiệm → liên lạc với bố mẹ → vài tính năng đơn giản → cảm giác trưởng thành.',tip:'Hai ý where/when got và when bought bị trùng trong tài liệu; bạn có thể trả lời gộp tự nhiên.',vocab:['save up|tiết kiệm để mua','keep in touch|giữ liên lạc','a sense of independence|cảm giác tự lập'],answer:`My first mobile phone was a small, basic phone with a physical keyboard. I bought it from a shop near my house when I was about sixteen. I had saved up some pocket money, and my parents paid the remaining amount.
The main reason I needed it was to keep in touch with my family. I had started attending extra classes after school, and sometimes the finishing time changed. Before I had a phone, my mother would wait outside without knowing when I would come out.
The phone couldn’t do much compared with the one I use today. I could make calls, send text messages and play a couple of simple games. It had a tiny screen, but the battery seemed to last for ages. I remember choosing a different ringtone almost every week because that felt exciting at the time.
When I first got it, I felt proud and surprisingly grown-up. It gave me a small sense of independence, although my parents reminded me not to use it during lessons.
I no longer have that phone, and I probably wouldn’t enjoy using it now. Still, I remember it fondly because it was one of the first things I helped pay for with my own money.`},
{title:'Nơi có những con vật thú vị',group:'Địa điểm',page:8,topic:'Describe a place you have visited where you can see interesting animals.',cues:['Why you went there','What the place looks like','What you did there','Which animals you found particularly interesting'],notes:['zoo · younger cousin','trees · ponds','walked · signs','giraffes → leaves'],vi:'Đi cùng em họ → mô tả không gian → các hoạt động → quan sát hươu cao cổ.',tip:'Chọn một loài và mô tả hành vi cụ thể thay vì đọc danh sách tên động vật.',vocab:['at my own pace|theo nhịp độ của mình','watch from a distance|quan sát từ xa','pay attention to|chú ý đến'],answer:`I’d like to talk about a zoo I visited with my younger cousin during a school holiday. He was very interested in animals, and I thought it would be a nice way for us to spend a morning together.
The place was larger and greener than I had expected. There were tall trees beside the paths, several ponds and benches where visitors could sit down. We arrived early, so it wasn’t too crowded, and we could explore at our own pace.
We walked around, read the information signs and took a few photographs. My cousin kept asking questions, and I soon discovered that I didn’t know as much about animals as I thought. Sometimes we had to read the signs together to find an answer.
The animals I found most interesting were the giraffes. I had seen pictures of them before, but seeing their height in real life was completely different. We watched from a distance as one of them reached up to eat leaves. Its movements were much slower and more careful than I expected.
What I enjoyed most was paying attention to small details instead of rushing from one area to another. The visit also gave my cousin and me something to talk about for the rest of the day.`},
{title:'Một thay đổi tích cực',group:'Thay đổi',page:9,topic:'Describe a positive change that you made to your life.',cues:['What the change is','Why it was important to make it','How you made the change','How important this positive change is'],notes:['phone away before bed','late nights → tired','charge outside bedroom','reading · calmer mornings'],vi:'Dùng điện thoại quá khuya → thay đổi môi trường → khó khăn ban đầu → tác động lên buổi sáng.',tip:'Khung trước – hành động – sau giúp đề change có mạch kể rõ ràng.',vocab:['cut down on|giảm bớt','out of reach|ngoài tầm với','stick to a habit|duy trì thói quen'],answer:`A positive change I made was putting my phone away before bedtime. It sounds like a small thing, but it has made my evenings much more enjoyable.
I used to spend a long time scrolling through videos after getting into bed. I would tell myself that I was only going to watch one more, but suddenly it would be past midnight. The next morning, I often felt tired and rushed to get ready for work.
I decided to change this by charging my phone outside my bedroom. I also bought a simple alarm clock, so I couldn’t use needing an alarm as an excuse. For the first few nights, I kept wanting to check my messages. To make the change easier, I left a book beside my bed and read a few pages instead.
I don’t follow this routine perfectly every day, especially at weekends, but I stick to it most of the time. I now have a clearer boundary between being online and resting.
This change is important to me because it has made my mornings feel less stressful. It also showed me that improving my routine doesn’t always require a big plan. Sometimes, changing one small thing in my environment makes a habit much easier to maintain.`},
{title:'Thay đổi để khỏe hơn',group:'Thay đổi',page:10,topic:'Describe a change you have made to improve your health and that you would recommend to others.',cues:['What it is','Why you decided to do it','How you have benefited','Why you would recommend it'],notes:['walk after work','sitting all day','start ten minutes','relaxed · easy routine'],vi:'Ngồi nhiều → đi bộ ngắn → tăng dần → cảm nhận cá nhân và lý do gợi ý.',tip:'Nói về trải nghiệm cá nhân bằng I feel…; không cần đưa ra các khẳng định y khoa.',vocab:['fit into my routine|phù hợp với lịch sinh hoạt','clear my head|giúp đầu óc thư thái','build up gradually|tăng dần từng chút'],answer:`One change I made to improve my health was going for a walk after work. I spend much of the day sitting at a desk, and I realised that I was barely moving between leaving home and getting back in the evening.
I decided to start small because I had tried ambitious exercise plans before and given up quickly. At first, I walked for about ten minutes around my neighbourhood. Once that felt normal, I gradually made the walks a little longer.
I usually go to a small park near my home. Sometimes I listen to music, but on other days I leave my headphones behind and just notice what is happening around me. A friend occasionally joins me, which makes it easier to keep the routine going.
The biggest benefit I have noticed is that I feel more relaxed afterwards. Walking gives me time to clear my head, so I’m less likely to keep thinking about work all evening. I also enjoy having a reason to spend time outdoors.
I would recommend trying a short walk to someone who wants a simple starting point for being more active. In my case, it costs nothing and fits easily into my routine. The key was finding something manageable rather than expecting myself to change everything at once.`},
{title:'Cuốn sách khiến bạn suy nghĩ',group:'Sách & báo',page:11,topic:'Describe a book that you enjoyed reading because you had to think a lot.',cues:['What the book was','Why you decided to read it','What it made you think about','Why you enjoyed reading it'],notes:['The Little Prince','friend recommended','adults · priorities','simple story → questions'],vi:'Sách Hoàng tử bé → bạn giới thiệu → suy nghĩ về điều quan trọng → ví dụ thay đổi cách nhìn.',tip:'Đề này hỏi suy nghĩ của bạn, nên dành phần lớn bài cho phản ứng cá nhân thay vì tóm tắt cốt truyện.',vocab:['take something for granted|coi điều gì là hiển nhiên','see things differently|nhìn sự việc khác đi','make time for|dành thời gian cho'],answer:`A book that made me think a lot was The Little Prince by Antoine de Saint-Exupéry. A friend recommended it to me, saying that although it looked like a children’s story, adults could get a lot from it too.
The story follows a little prince who travels to different places and meets various characters. The language in the version I read was fairly simple, so I expected to finish it quickly. However, I kept stopping to think about what the conversations meant.
In particular, it made me think about the things adults spend their time worrying about. I sometimes get so focused on finishing tasks and earning money that I forget to make time for people I care about. The book encouraged me to question whether being busy always means doing something important.
It also made me think about friendship. A relationship needs attention, even when two people already know each other well. After reading it, I called an old friend I hadn’t spoken to for months.
I enjoyed the book because it didn’t feel like a lecture. It used a simple story to raise questions that stayed in my mind afterwards. I would like to read it again in a few years and see whether I notice different things.`},
{title:'Báo hoặc tạp chí thường đọc',group:'Sách & báo',page:12,topic:'Describe a magazine or newspaper that you like to read.',cues:['What it is','What it is about','How often you read it','What kinds of people generally read it','Why you like reading it'],notes:['VnExpress · online','news · travel · daily life','lunch break','readers → my impression'],vi:'Báo điện tử → chủ đề → thói quen đọc → nhận xét thận trọng về độc giả → lợi ích.',tip:'Với điều không có số liệu, dùng I imagine… hoặc In my experience… thay vì nói như một sự thật chắc chắn.',vocab:['keep up with|theo dõi, cập nhật','catch my attention|thu hút sự chú ý','a starting point|một điểm khởi đầu'],answer:`An online newspaper I often read is VnExpress. I started reading it when I was a student, and it has remained part of my daily routine.
It covers a range of subjects, but I tend to choose articles about everyday life, travel and education. I don’t read every story on the homepage. Instead, I look through the headlines and open one or two articles that catch my attention.
I usually read it during my lunch break or while waiting for a bus. On weekdays, I might only spend ten minutes on it, whereas at weekends I sometimes read longer articles. I like being able to get a quick update without carrying a printed newspaper around.
I imagine it appeals to quite a broad group of readers, especially people who want news in Vietnamese on their phones. In my own family, both my father and I read it, although we choose very different sections.
The main reason I enjoy it is that it gives me things to discuss with friends and colleagues. Sometimes an article introduces a topic I want to learn more about. I treat it as a starting point, though, and if a story is particularly important to me, I try to compare it with other sources.`},
{title:'Cuốn sách thời thơ ấu',group:'Sách & báo',page:13,topic:'Describe a book you liked to read in your childhood.',cues:['Who wrote it','What it is about','When you read it','Why you liked it'],notes:['Dế Mèn phiêu lưu ký · Tô Hoài','cricket · adventures','primary school · gift','fun → responsibility'],vi:'Tên sách và tác giả → được tặng khi nhỏ → nội dung khái quát → niềm vui và bài học.',tip:'Dùng would + động từ để kể việc thường làm hồi nhỏ: I would read it before bed.',vocab:['bring a story to life|làm câu chuyện trở nên sống động','turn the page|lật sang trang tiếp','learn from mistakes|học từ sai lầm'],answer:`A book I loved as a child was Dế Mèn phiêu lưu ký, a story by the Vietnamese writer Tô Hoài. My aunt gave me a copy when I was in primary school, and I remember being attracted to the pictures before I even started reading.
The book is about a cricket and his adventures. Through the characters he meets and the problems he faces, the story explores friendship and learning to be more responsible. As a child, I mainly enjoyed the excitement of discovering what would happen next.
I would read a few pages before bed, and sometimes I asked my father to explain words I didn’t understand. The descriptions made the small world of insects feel like a much bigger place. I could imagine the characters moving through the grass as if I were there with them.
What I liked most was that the main character wasn’t perfect. He made mistakes and had to learn from them. That made him more interesting to me than a character who always did the right thing.
Looking back, the book gave me both entertainment and something to think about. I don’t remember every part of the plot now, but I still remember the feeling of wanting to turn the page. It helped me discover that reading could be an adventure in itself.`},
{title:'Kỳ nghỉ tuyệt vời nhất',group:'Chuyến đi',page:14,topic:'Describe the best holiday you ever had.',cues:['When and where you had it','How you got there','What you did and who you were with','Why it was special'],notes:['Da Nang · last summer','plane · parents','beach · seafood · photos','rare time together'],vi:'Đi Đà Nẵng cùng bố mẹ → hoạt động cụ thể → khoảnh khắc đáng nhớ → ý nghĩa gia đình.',tip:'Holiday nói về cả kỳ nghỉ; khác bài journey vốn nhấn mạnh hành trình di chuyển.',vocab:['quality time|thời gian bên nhau có ý nghĩa','a change of scenery|thay đổi không gian','in no hurry|không vội vàng'],answer:`The best holiday I’ve had was a short trip to Da Nang with my parents last summer. We flew there and stayed in a small hotel within walking distance of the beach.
We had only three days, so we decided not to fill our schedule with too many activities. On the first morning, we got up early and walked along the beach before it became hot. My father took far too many photographs, and we laughed because my mother kept telling him to put the camera down and enjoy the view.
Later, we tried local food, visited a market and spent a quiet afternoon at a café. My favourite moment was actually very simple: sitting by the sea after dinner and talking without looking at our phones. We were in no hurry to go anywhere.
The holiday was special because our schedules rarely allow us to spend that much time together. At home, we usually talk about practical things, such as work or what to buy for dinner. During the trip, we shared stories and enjoyed each other’s company.
It wasn’t an expensive or adventurous holiday, but it gave us a welcome change of scenery. When I think about it now, I remember how relaxed we felt rather than the places we visited.`},
{title:'Kỳ nghỉ lý tưởng',group:'Chuyến đi',page:15,topic:'Describe your idea of a perfect vacation.',cues:['Where it would be','Who would be with you','What you would do there','Why it would be perfect for you'],notes:['Da Lat · close friends','small guesthouse','walks · coffee · no packed schedule','rest + connection'],vi:'Kỳ nghỉ giả định ở Đà Lạt → người đi cùng → lịch nhẹ nhàng → lý do phù hợp với bạn.',tip:'Giữ would cho kỳ nghỉ tưởng tượng. Không chuyển cả bài sang quá khứ như thể đã đi.',vocab:['a packed schedule|lịch trình kín','switch off|tạm gác công việc để thư giãn','leave room for|chừa thời gian hoặc chỗ cho'],answer:`My idea of a perfect vacation would be a few days in Da Lat with two close friends. I wouldn’t need a luxury hotel or a long list of attractions. A comfortable guesthouse in a quiet area would suit me perfectly.
I’d choose these friends because we enjoy a similar pace of travel. None of us likes getting up extremely early just to rush between famous places. We would probably plan one main activity each day and leave the rest of the time open.
In the mornings, I’d like to go for a walk and find somewhere simple for breakfast. We could spend an afternoon at a café, reading or chatting, and perhaps visit a garden if the weather was pleasant. I would also enjoy taking photographs without feeling that I had to post everything online immediately.
This would be perfect for me because my normal working week is quite structured. I often have deadlines and messages to answer, so on holiday I want the freedom to decide what to do as the day goes on.
Of course, no trip is perfect in every detail. It might rain, or a café might be closed. But with good company and a flexible plan, those small problems wouldn’t matter very much. The main aim would be to rest and reconnect.`},
{title:'Hoạt động muốn thử ở biển',group:'Trải nghiệm',page:16,topic:'Describe a leisure activity near or on the sea that you want to try.',cues:['What it is','What you need to prepare','How easy or difficult it is','Why you want to try it'],notes:['kayaking · guided lesson','life jacket · sunscreen','balance · paddling','new view of coast'],vi:'Muốn chèo kayak → chuẩn bị và hướng dẫn → khó khăn dự kiến → lý do thích.',tip:'Dùng I expect / I imagine để thể hiện đây là dự đoán về trải nghiệm chưa thử.',vocab:['give it a try|thử làm điều gì','get the hang of it|dần biết cách làm','step out of my comfort zone|thử điều ngoài vùng quen thuộc'],answer:`A seaside activity I would like to try is kayaking. I’ve seen people paddling close to the shore while I was on holiday, and it looked like an interesting way to enjoy the sea.
Since I’ve never done it before, I would book a beginner session with an instructor. I would need a suitable life jacket, comfortable clothes and protection from the sun. I’d also check the conditions with the organiser and follow their instructions about where to go. I wouldn’t want my first attempt to be on my own.
I imagine the basic movements might be fairly easy to learn, but keeping a steady direction could be harder than it looks. I would probably get tired quite quickly at first because I’m not used to paddling. Still, I think I could get the hang of it with some patient guidance.
The main reason I want to try it is that it would let me see the coastline from a different angle. Usually, I just sit on the beach or walk beside the water. Being out on the sea would make the experience more active and memorable.
I’d like to go with a friend so we could encourage each other. Even if I turned out to be rather slow, I think I would enjoy learning something new and stepping out of my comfort zone.`}
];
